🧠 What is the OSI Model?

The OSI model is a conceptual framework that standardizes communication functions into 7 layers:

Physical
Data Link
Network
Transport
Session
Presentation
Application
💬 Telegram Message Flow (Layer by Layer)
7️⃣ Application Layer
User interacts with the Telegram app (mobile/desktop/web)
Message is typed and sent
Telegram uses its own protocol: MTProto

👉 Handles:

User interface
Message creation
API communication
6️⃣ Presentation Layer
Data is encrypted before transmission
Telegram uses strong encryption (MTProto protocol)

👉 Handles:

Encryption / Decryption
Data formatting
5️⃣ Session Layer
Establishes and maintains connection between client and Telegram servers

👉 Handles:

Session authentication
Connection persistence
4️⃣ Transport Layer
Ensures reliable data delivery
Telegram primarily uses TCP (sometimes UDP for calls)

👉 Handles:

Segmentation
Error checking
Flow control
3️⃣ Network Layer
Determines the path of the data across networks

👉 Handles:

IP addressing
Routing (via routers)
2️⃣ Data Link Layer
Transfers data between devices on the same network

👉 Handles:

MAC addressing
Frame transmission
Error detection (CRC)
1️⃣ Physical Layer
Actual transmission of raw bits over hardware

👉 Examples:

Wi-Fi signals 📶
Ethernet cables 🔌
Cellular networks 📡
